ticket.body_markdown:
**Type:** Improvement · **Component:** SQL

### Motivation

Sort is a very resource-intensive operation. Spark may add SortExec when writing partition files for writing sequentially, but sorting is unnecessary when there is only one partition. The ordering check in `org.apache.spark.sql.execution.datasources.FileFormatWriter` (shown below) does not account for the single-partition case, so an unnecessary SortExec can be added.

```java
// We should first sort by partition columns, then bucket id, and finally sorting columns.
val requiredOrdering = partitionColumns ++ bucketIdExpression ++ sortColumns
// the sort order doesn't matter
val actualOrdering = plan.outputOrdering.map(_.child)
val orderingMatched = if (requiredOrdering.length > actualOrdering.length) {
  false
} else {
  requiredOrdering.zip(actualOrdering).forall {
    case (requiredOrder, childOutputOrder) =>
      requiredOrder.semanticEquals(childOutputOrder)
  }
}
```

### Proposed behavior

FileFormatWriter should skip the sort when there is only one partition, avoiding the unnecessary SortExec.

### Acceptance criteria

_Not provided_

