``` and arguments str (string type), delimiter (string type), partNum (Integer type). Behavior: splits str by delimiter and returns the requested part (1-based); if any input parameter is NULL, returns NULL; if the index is out of range of split parts, returns empty string; if partNum is 0, throws an error; if partNum is negative, parts are counted backward from the end of the string; when delimiter is empty, str is considered not split thus there is just 1 split part. Examples: ```java
